      "solution": "idx = int(input())\ns = list(input().strip())\nfor i in [idx - 1, idx, idx + 1]:\n    if 0 <= i < len(s):\n        s[i] = \"1\" if s[i] == \"0\" else \"0\"\nprint(\"\".join(s))\n",
      "statement": "Given an integer [[index]] and a binary string [[binaryString]], apply an inversion wave centered at [[index]].\n\nFlip the bit at [[index]] and any existing adjacent neighbors (`index - 1` and `index + 1`).\n- A `'0'` flips to `'1'`\n- A `'1'` flips to `'0'`\n\nAll other bits remain untouched. If a neighbor index falls outside the string bounds, ignore it.",
